      "text": "1905: Fauvism (Paris) -- Matisse, Derain, Vlaminck\n        Color completely unchained from description\n                    |\n  1905: Die Brücke (Dresden) -- Expressionism\n        Kirchner, Heckel, Nolde\n                    |\n  1908-1913: CUBISM (Paris) -- Picasso / Braque\n        Analytic Cubism (1908-1912):\n          Multiple simultaneous viewpoints, monochrome\n        Synthetic Cubism (1912-1914):\n          Collage, papier collé, newspaper fragments\n                    |\n  1909: Futurism (Italy) -- Marinetti manifesto\n        Boccioni, Severini, Balla\n        Speed, machine, dynamism, violence\n                    |\n  1910: Der Blaue Reiter (Munich) -- Kandinsky / Marc\n        Inner necessity, toward pure abstraction\n                    |\n  1913: Armory Show (New York) -- European modernism\n        hits the American public\n                    |\n  1916: DADA (Zurich / Berlin / New York / Paris)\n        Tzara, Arp, Ball, Hausmann, Duchamp\n        Anti-art, anti-war, institutional critique\n                    |\n  1924: Surrealism (Paris) -- Breton's First Manifesto\n        Ernst, Dalí, Magritte, Kahlo, Miro"
    },
