      "text": "WHAT FAUVISM DOES TO COLOR:\n  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ Before Fauvism: even Impressionism and Post-Impressionism │\n  │ related color to observation. Seurat: scientific.         │\n  │ Van Gogh: emotionally heightened but still FROM the scene.│\n  │                                                           │\n  │ Fauvism: color is AUTONOMOUS.                             │\n  │                                                           │\n  │ The skin can be green.                                    │\n  │ The shadow can be red.                                    │\n  │ The road can be pink.                                     │\n  │ Color is chosen for its PICTORIAL function --             │\n  │ its relation to other colors, its expressive energy --    │\n  │ NOT for its descriptive accuracy.                         │\n  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
