      "text": "- **Dance (1909–1910, Hermitage)**: five figures, circle, primary red-orange + blue +\n  green, almost no space — pure form and movement\n- **The Red Studio (1911)**: the studio as red field — everything absorbed into red;\n  the artworks depicted are identifiable but flattened into the surface\n- **Cut-outs (1940s–1954)**: after surgery, unable to paint standing; colored paper\n  cut and arranged — Jazz (1947), The Snail (1953). The cut-out technique eliminates\n  the distinction between drawing and color: \"cutting directly into color\""
