      "text": "- **Kandinsky**: on the path to pure abstraction (see module 08-ABSTRACTION.md);\n  the goal is spiritual expression through pure visual elements without reference\n  to the physical world\n- **Marc**: animals as subjects — horses as pure being, uncorrupted by human\n  consciousness; Blue Horse I (1911); the Tower of Blue Horses (1913, lost)\n- **Der Blaue Reiter Almanac (1912)**: the key document — Kandinsky and Marc compile\n  essays and images juxtaposing folk art, Bavarian glass painting, African masks,\n  medieval woodcuts, and modern work — the canon-leveling act: all is equally valid\n  evidence of spiritual necessity in visual form"
