      "text": "1. **Cézanne's retrospective (Salon d'Automne, 1907)**: 56 paintings, a year after\n   his death. Braque and Picasso both attend repeatedly.\n2. **African and Iberian sculpture**: Picasso sees masks in the Trocadéro museum (1907)\n   that he later describes as a revelation about non-European formal possibilities.\n3. **Les Demoiselles d'Avignon (1907)**: usually cited as the proto-Cubist painting\n   — five women (proto-Cubist formal vocabulary), the right two with faces influenced\n   by African masks. The painting was not exhibited until 1916 — it was a studio\n   working-out, not a public statement."
    },
